-- A loan belongs to one member. A member has a late loan when one of its loans is due before
-- today. Rule MoveLoan gives a loan to another member when a Transfer arrives, by setting the
-- loan's `member`.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", exactly two lines about MemberWithLateLoan:
--
--   ### Member
--   - A new Loan can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateLoan.
--   - Time passing can now make a Member become a MemberWithLateLoan.
--
-- A line is missing. Moving a late loan makes its receiver a MemberWithLateLoan and can make the
-- member it left stop being one, and the report says neither. The compiler does not count a
-- write of `Loan.member` as a change to `Member.loans`, which is the same records read from
-- the other side.
act Member { name: text }

act Loan {
    member: one Member
    dueOn: Date
}

transient act Transfer {
    loan: one Loan
    receiver: one Member
}

rule MoveLoan when Transfer {
    loan.member = receiver
}

shape MemberWithLateLoan = Member where exists (loans where dueOn < today)
